transmed:TMO_0036 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> "A cell line is a material entity that consists of a population of cells cultured in vitro that are descended through one or more generations (and possible sub-cultures) from a single primary culture which was originally derived from part of an organism."@en;
                  <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "EFO:0000322",
